## What We Are Building

Pure design/planning session. Two approved plans live in
`~/.claude/plans/workstation-reference-designerdesigner-r-twinkling-hamming.md` (ONE file, TWO plans):

- **Plan 1 — version-editor (slice 0).** Single universal window for ALL text artifacts (ref_plan,
  brief, script, storyboard, review, series idea, prompts). Access to ALL versions (not just latest),
  manual edit where **save = new REVIEW version** (never overwrites the row), and per-version lifecycle
  buttons: Approve / Reject / un-approve. Un-approve is a 3-way fork: (a) rework manually (no agent),
  (b) send to stage critic, (c) send to producer (existing REQUEST_REVISION auto-chain). Anti-additive:
  ~80% already exists (each version already a separate `assets` row; status graph already allows
  APPROVED→REVISION etc.; CodeMirror EditorModal + approve API exist). Net ≈ 0 LoC (deletes
  GeneralIdeaEditor, −163).

- **Plan 2 — shot-centric refactor.** Invert UX from executor-centric to shot-centric. ONE video-animatic
  timeline = persistent home grid, renders EARLY from storyboard shot_list (before any video/animatic);
  each cell = live shot state (starfield placeholder → ref → anchor → preview video → final); click →
  persistent per-shot dossier embedding the Plan-1 version-editor. Drop the duplicate "reference animatic"
  gallery (fold into timeline cells; re-home EREF review under PreviewDrawer). Per-shot video unblocks the
  moment a shot has ref/anchors (provider by availability) — not gated on whole-episode refs. Animatic
  PRESERVED as the final-assembly contract STITCH reads (timing/audio). Slices A→B→C→D; D depends on Plan 1.

