## Decisions Made

- **Save = new REVIEW version** (q1, corrected) — old APPROVED stays live until explicit re-approve; zero
  silent replacement; no demote-on-save.
- **Editor scope = text artifacts only** (q2) — structured forms (ShotPlanContract, EREFv2 verdict) + binaries
  stay in their viewers.
- **Un-approve = 3-way fork** (q3) — manual / critic / producer; manual default, no agent re-fire.
- **Un-approve via separate `/status` PATCH route** — NOT a new approve decision (avoids touching approve
  route's 200-line side-effects); structurally has no inngest.send.
- **Two animatics → one** — video-animatic timeline is the superset; reference gallery is a pure visual dup;
  STITCH already sources VID-animatic; animatic stays as final-assembly contract.
- **Per-shot video eligibility** — relax episode-wide ANIMATIC_APPROVED gate to per-shot readiness; early
  video = preview, final cut still assembled from locked animatic.
- **Both plans parked until after прогон** — Director's standing instruction.

